= Conclusion <sec:conclusion>

#refine[]
In attempt to answer the research question 
(although @sec:results needs polish to back this up properly):
@SC:lo has high potential for real-time generation of large 
and realistic trees at various @LOD:s.

#refine[]
Most techniques mentioned in this paper need to be part of 
a bigger system to give proper contrast to up-sides and down-sides.
These algorithms are rarely usable straight out-of-the-box, 
even less so for custom engines or frameworks.

#refine[]
With the advent of diffusion models and other artificial intelligence techniques, 
it remains to be demonstrated whether classical solutions like noise functions 
and L-systems will stand their ground in procedural generation against 
infinite diffusion (#todo[turn into ref: https://xandergos.github.io/terrain-diffusion/]).
